@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the eight failing e2e tests, their root causes, and what each one is waiting on
' covers: tests/e2e/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh
'
' Measured: `go test -tags=e2e ./tests/e2e/` on this host — 35 pass, 6 skip, 8 fail,
' 585s. Every failure reproduces on a pristine checkout, so none of them is a
' regression from the decomposition; they are the baseline that has to be repaired
' before move 6 (_spec/_plans/main-decomposition-moves.puml) can be judged.
'
' ── C1 · RESOLVED — TWO BUGS ON ONE LINE, AND TWO WRONG EXPLANATIONS ───────
' The line C1 accused really is defective. Neither explanation offered for it was
' right, including the correction that replaced the first one.
'
'     exec 9>"${dir}/install.lock" 2>/dev/null || return 0
'
' WRONG #1 (original C1): "a failed redirect on `exec` is fatal to a
' non-interactive shell, so `|| return 0` is dead code". Measured against a path
' even root cannot open for writing, under `set -euo pipefail`, on bash 4.4, 5.0
' and 5.2: the shell does NOT exit and the guard fires. Bash only exits there in
' POSIX mode, which the entrypoint never sets.
'
' WRONG #2 (the first correction): "the trace ending on `+ exec` is a stdout /
' stderr interleaving artifact." It is not an artifact. It is the bug.
'
' RIGHT: a bare `exec` — one with no command — applies its redirections to the
' SHELL, permanently. `2>/dev/null` therefore did not scope stderr to the exec; it
' discarded stderr for the rest of the entrypoint AND for the agent the entrypoint
' goes on to exec. `set -x` writes to stderr, which is exactly why every trace
' ended on `+ exec` and why so many failures in this harness presented as a silent
' death with no message. The output was never produced late or out of order. It
' was thrown away.
' _proveo_unlock_installs carried the identical defect: `exec 9>&- 2>/dev/null`.
'
' FIX (this is C1's original proposal, correct for a different reason):
'     if ! : >>"${dir}/install.lock" 2>/dev/null; then return 0; fi
'     exec 9>>"${dir}/install.lock"
' and `_proveo_unlock_installs() { exec 9>&-; }`.
'
' WHAT IT WAS HIDING · with stderr restored, one trace found the real abort in a
' second: `_node_json_field` runs `node -e` and the cecli image ships python and
' NO node, so it returned 127 — assigned in a command substitution under
' `set -euo pipefail`, which ends the run. The same family as
' _node_version_file (_spec/internal/sbx/seed-node-version-abort.puml): absence
' reported as failure.
'
' All 24 helpers whose results are command-substituted were then audited by
' MEASUREMENT inside the image, not by reading. Exactly two were non-zero:
' _node_json_field (127, no node) and _proveo_github_token (1, `pipefail` plus an
' unauthenticated `gh auth token`). Both now return 0; the other 22 already did.
'
' RESULT · TestHelloWorldE2E goes green, both failing legs. cecli 6.17s-fail ->
' 21.5s-pass, and claudecode's "the agent surfaced no model answer" was the
' agent's own stderr going to /dev/null.
'
' The lesson this file already taught twice, now three times: a mechanism argued
' from an artifact is a guess. Two confident explanations were built on `+ exec`
' before anyone tested what that line does to fd 2.

' ── C2 · DONE · ASSERTIONS NOW PIN THE CURRENT CONTRACT ────────────────────
' sbxHome DELETES HOME and PROVEO_HOME on the sandbox backend and publishes
' PROVEO_STATE_HOME instead. That deletion IS the fix: redirecting HOME orphaned
' the credential sbx's own proxy writes under the image's home, and the agent then
' reported "Not logged in". Three tests still assert the redirect:
'   TestProveoHomePersistence ("agent cmd missing -e HOME=")
'   TestSandboxKitIsAMixinCarryingNoCredentials ("Kit environment omits HOME")
'   TestSandboxBackendCarriesProveoHomeBesideHome (the name is the old contract)
' APPLIED. Each now asserts the CURRENT contract: no HOME/PROVEO_HOME in the sbx
' argv or Kit, PROVEO_STATE_HOME present and an ABSOLUTE HOST path, and the docker
' path unchanged — plus a guard that the redirect cannot return by accident. Not a
' loosening: every one gained a positive claim it did not have. The third was
' renamed, because its old name WAS the retired contract:
'   TestSandboxBackendCarriesProveoHomeBesideHome
'     -> TestSandboxBackendPublishesStateHomeAndNoRedirect
'
' ── C3 · TWO FAILURES ENCODE OPEN DECISIONS — DO NOT MAKE THEM GREEN ────────
' These two are the live evidence behind _spec/_plans/revision-env-egress.puml.
' Flipping either to match today's behaviour would erase the finding.
'
'   TestEveryHarnessGetsTheDockerAccessItPromises  (decision D2)
'     asserts no socket and no daemon inside an sbx sandbox; the probe reports
'     HAS-SOCKET and SERVER:29.7.2 for claudecode and cursor, because the images
'     now carry com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker. Code and test assert opposite
'     things about one decision. It goes green when D2 is decided: either the
'     label is gated like dind, or this assertion is rewritten to "a daemon is
'     present AND its containers cannot leave the Kit allowlist".
'
'   TestCredentialForwardingIntegrity  (decision D1) — NOW GREEN, measured.
'     It is listed here as red; it passes. Re-measure before acting on this entry.
'     asserts no provider key appears in the sandbox argv; proveo deliberately
'     emits `-e VAR=` (empty) to override sbx's GLOBAL secret store. The empty
'     value is also how a workspace .env refills a variable proveo blanked. It
'     goes green when D1 lands: assert `-e VAR=` carries no VALUE, and add the
'     sentinel parity the plan proposes.
'
' ── C4 · DONE · AND IT WAS NOT ENVIRONMENTAL ────────────────────────────────
' The suspicion here was macOS: outside open+forward the local-model posture drops
' to a CPU-only sidecar, slow enough to look like a hang. It was not that. The test
' already runs `--egress-mode open --credentials forward` with PROVEO_SBX=off, so
' it always reached the HOST's Ollama and the theory was ruled out by construction.
' Both failing legs were C1's discarded stderr. The legs named here were also
' wrong: opencode PASSED throughout; cecli and claudecode were the red ones.
' TestPromptfulE2E was green before any of this work.
' Nothing needed a posture fix or a longer deadline.
'
' ── ACCEPTANCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Green does NOT mean zero red. It means: C1 and C2 pass, C4 passes or states a
' measured environmental reason, and the only red left is C3 — where each failure
' names the decision it is waiting on. A suite in that state is a baseline a
' refactor can be judged against, because every red has an owner.
title DONE — a readable e2e baseline: C1 + C2 + C4 fixed, only C3 red by design

component "go test -tags=e2e ./tests/e2e/\nWAS 35 pass · 6 skip · 8 fail\nNOW 47 pass · 8 skip · 1 fail (C3, by design)" as SUITE <<app>>

frame "C1 · RESOLVED — and the cause named here was wrong" as C1 <<host>> {
  component "_proveo_lock_installs was NOT it\n`exec 9>` does not exit the shell:\nmeasured on bash 4.4 / 5.0 / 5.2" as LOCK <<app>>
  component "_node_version_file, missing `return 0`\nfixed; the blocked test now passes" as FIXLOCK <<app>>
}

frame "C2 · assertions pin a retired contract" as C2 <<host>> {
  component "3 tests assert -e HOME=\nsbxHome deletes it on purpose" as HOMEA <<error>>
  component "assert PROVEO_STATE_HOME instead,\nand that the redirect stays gone" as FIXHOME <<app>>
}

frame "C3 · decision-bearing, keep red" as C3 <<host>> {
  component "docker access promise (D2)\nHAS-SOCKET · SERVER:29.7.2" as D2 <<error>>
  component "credential argv (D1)\n`-e VAR=` is deliberate" as D1 <<error>>
}

frame "C4 · measure again after C1" as C4 <<host>> {
  component "HelloWorld · Promptful\nlocal model, CPU sidecar on macOS" as MODEL <<async>>
}

LOCK ARROW_OPTIONAL SUITE : no longer red
SUITE ARROW_ERROR HOMEA
SUITE ARROW_ERROR D2
SUITE ARROW_ERROR D1
FIXLOCK ARROW_MAIN LOCK : the real line
HOMEA ARROW_MAIN FIXHOME
FIXLOCK ARROW_QUEUE MODEL : re-measured — HelloWorld still red
D2 ARROW_OPTIONAL SUITE : green when D2 lands
D1 ARROW_OPTIONAL SUITE : green when D1 lands

note bottom of LOCK
  Proven by measurement, not by reading: installs
  on gives exit 1 in one second with the trace
  ending on `+ exec`; installs off reaches
  PROVEO_SMOKE_READY and holds.
end note

note bottom of FIXHOME
  A rewrite, not a loosening. Each of the three
  gains a positive claim it lacked — that
  PROVEO_STATE_HOME points at the mounted home and
  that the old redirect cannot come back.
end note

note bottom of C3
  Both reds are findings. Matching them to today's
  behaviour deletes the only evidence that the
  sandbox ships a daemon, and that a blanked
  credential can be refilled from the workspace.
end note

note bottom of SUITE
  The bar is not zero red. It is: every red names
  the decision it waits on. That is a baseline a
  refactor can be judged against, because a new
  failure is then unmistakable.
end note
@enduml
